Camera-mount static TF + librealsense SDK pin for the VLN on the Fly airframe.

This is a RECORD of how realsense-ros in this repository diverges from the
upstream release it was taken from. It is NOT applied at build time -- the
patched sources are vendored under realsense-ros/. Keep this file in sync when
the driver is touched, and use it to rebase onto a future upstream release.

Upstream base : IntelRealSense/realsense-ros tag 4.57.7
Diverges in   : realsense2_camera only

1. Camera-mount static transform.
   The D435i is bolted to the airframe, not described by a URDF, so nothing
   published base_link -> camera_link. Goal projection needs that transform to
   turn a VLM-grounded pixel region into a world-frame point. Adds parameters:
     publish_mount_tf       (bool,   default false -- off unless asked for)
     mount_parent_frame_id  (string, default "base_link")
     mount_x, mount_y, mount_z          (double, metres)
     mount_roll, mount_pitch, mount_yaw (double, radians)
   When publish_mount_tf is false the driver behaves exactly like upstream.

2. librealsense SDK pin lowered 2.57.7 -> 2.56.6 in CMakeLists.txt, to match
   the librealsense2 build installed on the Jetson Orin NX image.

